---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
import { getAllTopics } from '../lib/topics';
import { href } from '../lib/url';

const topics = await getAllTopics();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Layer 8: guided courses and field notes for networking, scripting, Linux, and security."
>
  <div class="narrow">
    <header class="page-head">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> About</span>
      <h1>A notebook for the layers beneath the app.</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose" style="padding-bottom:40px">
      <p>
        <strong>{SITE.name}</strong> is a reading-first library about the parts of
        computing that are easy to use and hard to explain: packets, names,
        processes, shells, and the trust boundaries between them.
      </p>

      <p>
        Guides are built as ordered paths through a topic. Notes are the smaller
        pieces: something broke, I learned why, and I wrote down the part I would
        want to find next time. The goal is not to cover everything. It is to make
        a small number of ideas genuinely clear.
      </p>

      <h2>What you will find here</h2>

      <ul>
        {topics.map((topic) => (
          <li>
            <strong>{topic.label}</strong> — {topic.description}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <h2>How to read it</h2>

      <p>
        Start with a guide when you want the full path, or use the search bar on
        the home page when you need a specific answer. Notes are filed by topic
        rather than by date, so a single area reads like a short course. Each
        piece ends with related material if you want to keep going.
      </p>

      <h2>Who writes this</h2>

      <p>
        {SITE.author}. I work with systems, networks, and automation, and I prefer
        diagrams and small experiments to buzzwords. You can find the code and
        corrections on <a href={SITE.github} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        The best documentation is the note you wrote for yourself six months ago.
      </blockquote>
    </div>

    <div style="display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;padding-bottom:60px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={href('/guides/')}>
        Start a guide <Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} />
      </a>
      <a class="btn" href={href('/topics/notes/')}>Read the notes</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
